    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ae859bd791a832530b6ce64e18c37fc67dcb0d67bb7360ece3ee07ab034d0d0e",
      "text": "Day 3 · Breakfast. At the scheduled time, meet your guide at the hotel and transfer to the railway station for the train to Aguas Calientes, then a guided visit of Machu Picchu. Built by the emperor Pachacútec as a royal estate and sacred retreat, with a palace complex, noble residences and temples, the citadel stands at 2,450 metres and was never found by the Spanish conquerors. Long hidden, it was brought to international attention in 1911 by the American explorer Hiram Bingham; its perfectly fitted stonework and earthquake-resistant terraces still amaze engineers today. A UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1983, it was named one of the New Seven Wonders of the World in 2007. In the afternoon, descend to Aguas Calientes for lunch at the traditional El Mapi restaurant, then return by train to Cusco and transfer to the hotel.",
